Open Vanilla: Herald's brain (playerbot/HeraldBrain.*) and upstream bot-AI fixes

Herald is the bot AI playing a real player's own character (the self-bot: master == bot and a real
session). Random and alt bots never enter this code. On top of 0016's pull rules:
- a fight predictor with a risk budget decides each pull (HeraldMath.h, tested in realm/mangos/tests);
  in a group a player made, in dungeons and battlegrounds the bot AI's own choices stand;
- stuck recovery in steps after 25 s / 70 s / 150 s instead of 5 minutes, only while he walks to a
  travel target out in the world (not at the bank, in a dungeon or in a player's group);
- grouping with another Herald for a shared group quest or the same quest mobs; invite, accept and
  leave are queued on their own sessions as the client's packets, so the world thread runs them;
- gray-only selling and repairs at a vendor he stands next to;
- memory of where and to what he died (an hour, not in dungeons);
- a fight log and stuck log (openvanilla_herald_fight / _stuck, classicplus_herald_ai.sql);
- one line per choice for the Herald panel (an OVH: whisper to his own client only).
Also: FleeManager tested every ring at the maximum distance and could step off ledges; and eleven
upstream cmangos/playerbots fixes (Sep-Oct 2026) cherry-picked onto the pinned 31e0f32: stuck
hearthstone, loot/travel back-and-forth loops, unreachable destinations, no grinding on long trips,
paths on non-instance maps, jump/knockback, loot stutter, ClipPath iterator, mobs that won't attack.
Applies after 0016 and 0017.

